\section{What-If Rescheduling}
\textbf{Rule.} At 05:00, add a buffer of $B$ minutes to the scheduled arrival of every flight the model flags. \textbf{Assumptions.} (A1) Padding moves the published arrival time, not the landing, so a padded flight is late only if $\text{arr\_delay} - B \geq 15$. (A2) No knock-on effects on the aircraft's next flight, crews, gates or connections. (A3) The cost is the buffer minutes added, and every policy gets the same budget; a minute is ``used'' if the flight was at least that late. (A4) Actual test-month delays only score the policy offline; the flags use 05:00 information only, as test labels score a model. (A5) Cancelled and diverted flights have no arrival time and are left out.

\textbf{Same budget, four policies.} The budget is the hybrid's rule-(b) flag count, <<n(d10['k_flagged'])>> of <<n(d10['n_test'])>> test flights, $\times$ <<d10['buffer_min']>> minutes. Each score pads its own top <<n(d10['k_flagged'])>> flights; random flights (mean of 200 draws) are the floor (Table~\ref{tab:policy}). The hybrid's flags avoid <<f"{pol['hybrid flags']['late arrivals avoided']:.0f}">> late arrivals, logistic regression's <<f"{pol['logistic regression flags']['late arrivals avoided']:.0f}">>, the planner's 28-day rule <<f"{pol['planner rule (28-day rate)']['late arrivals avoided']:.0f}">> and random flights <<f"{pol['random flights']['late arrivals avoided']:.0f}">>; <<f"{100 * pol['hybrid flags']['share of buffer minutes used']:.1f}">>\% of the hybrid's buffer minutes are used, against <<f"{100 * pol['random flights']['share of buffer minutes used']:.1f}">>\% for random flags. The gap to random is the value the risk score adds; the gap between the models is small, as in the test table.

\textbf{Buffer size.} Larger buffers avoid more late arrivals but each extra minute buys less (Table~\ref{tab:sweep}, Fig.~\ref{fig:whatif}): <<sweep[5]['late arrivals avoided']>> avoided at 5 minutes, <<sweep[60]['late arrivals avoided']>> at 60, while <<n(sweep[15]['padded but on time anyway'])>> padded flights would have been on time anyway at every buffer size.

